      "content": "That feeling of everything dissolving is a profound kind of exhaustion, not just sadness. When the future loses its shape, it's easier to just stop moving through it. If the whole script feels finished, maybe you can just let the character take a break, for a while. You don't have to force a new scene to start; sometimes just letting the static run is enough.",
      "source": "target",
